<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Pioneer to pay A$5 mln penalties.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Pioneer to pay A$5 mln penalties.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Competition and Consumer Commission said on Friday that penalties and costs of A$5 million had been awarded against building products group Pioneer International Ltd and a subsidiary following a trade practices case in the Federal Court.</p>
<p>The regulator said it had brought an action against the company after it acquired a competitor in south Queensland which had the effect of substantially lessening competition in that market.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
